      "worked": "All angles are in radians. For $0<u<\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, unit-circle geometry gives $\\sin u<u$: the vertical side is shorter than the corresponding circular arc, whose length is $u$.\n\nSince $0<\\cos(1)<1<\\frac{\\pi}{2}$,\n$$\\sin(\\cos(1))<\\cos(1).$$\nSince $0<\\sin(1)<1$ and cosine decreases on $[0,\\pi]$,\n$$\\cos(\\sin(1))>\\cos(1).$$\nTherefore $\\cos(\\sin(1))$ is larger.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
